  "reason": "The current best (config_036: SCVI + ViT-L + multiprofile + avgpool + concat, acc 0.715) establishes that a learned RNA encoder (SCVI) combined with a strong image encoder (ViT-L) is the dominant design choice. However, SCGPT—a generative single-cell model that may capture different biological structure than SCVI—has not been tested in any experiment. Config_048 isolates this single variable (SCGPT vs SCVI) while holding all other settings at their proven-best values (ViT-L, multiprofile, avgpool, concat), making it directly comparable to config_036. This is the highest-information next step: if SCGPT outperforms SCVI, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms SCVI as the optimal RNA encoder and lets us redirect effort toward aggregation or fusion refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving this untested encoder dimension is more valuable than testing a second-order variable (e.g., transformer vs avgpool) where existing evidence already favors avgpool."
}

